What tier A cannot see is the modulation itself: the extent table is
not an argument, so \code{E_u(t0) / E_u(t0) = 1} is verified by
\code{\link[=backcast_admin_shares]{backcast_admin_shares()}}'s own tests, not here. The last check is the
one that catches a \code{shares_backcast} and a \code{seams} built from
different runs -- and a deliberate \verb{seam =} override, which moves \code{t0}
